# =============================================================================
# mimo-v2.6-flash-rl_rank.env.example -- XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.6-Flash-RL on a
# 2-node DGX Spark pair (TP=2), served by an aarch64/sm_121 image from
# build-spark-cu132.sh (local-inference-lab/vllm dev/karmic-kraken @ e77be225
# + local-inference-lab/b12x @ 8a99d639 -- the kk-beta-cu132 profile) PLUS
# liburing-dev (Dockerfile.io-uring -> local/vllm:karmic-kraken-beta-cu132-io-uring).
# Launcher: mimo-v2.6-flash-rl_pair-serve.sh
#
# Checkpoint: XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.6-Flash-RL @ 3b38d063 (config.json,
#   verified 2026-09-23): MiMoV2ForCausalLM, 309B total / 15B active, 48
#   layers = 9 global-attention + 39 SWA (window 128, SWA sink bias),
#   hidden 4096, head_dim 192 QK / 128 V; GA 64 Q / 4 KV heads, SWA 64 / 8;
#   256 routed experts, top-8, sigmoid router. Quantization: quant_method
#   fp8 (block 128x128, dynamic activations) with store_dtype mxfp4 for the
#   experts; o_proj layers kept BF16. NOT ModelOpt. num_nextn_predict_layers
#   3 (in-checkpoint MTP). max_position 1,048,576. Vision ViT (28 layers) +
#   audio tokenizer/encoder (audio via the MiMoV2OmniForCausalLM override).
#   NO mamba/GDN/recurrent state -- pure-attention hybrid.
# KV cost (derived, BF16, TP2): only the 9 GA layers grow with context:
#   2 KV heads/rank x (192+128) x 2 B x 9 = 11,520 B/token/rank -> 1M tokens
#   ~= 11.0 GiB per rank. The 39 SWA layers hold a fixed ~128-token window
#   per request (tens of MB). 1,048,576 context is cheap on this model.
#
# GROUNDWORK STATUS (2026-09-23): the catalog (lil.yaml) qualifies MiMo at
# TP4 on SM120 ONLY (requires arch sm_120a) with b12x loading. GB10/sm_121a
# is UNQUALIFIED territory -- Luke and Dooner serve it, not this pair; every
# value below is the vendor contract (lil.yaml + Luke's serve-mimo26-flash.sh),
# not a measurement. Bring-up order at the file tail; record results in the
# header as they land.
#
# The b12x loader is the ONLY validated path for this checkpoint (vllm
# de16d7413 / 308fb7204: MiMo router/vision/audio weights allocated through
# the loader pool; Luke's serve-mimo26-flash.sh defaults to it). On Spark it
# reads weights through a 16 MiB O_DIRECT io_uring bounce ring (b12x 1ec67ef,
# in 8a99d639). Three things must hold, all checked by --check:
#   1. the IMAGE has liburing-dev (b12x compiles its native reader at first
#      use; without liburing: "io_uring bounce support is unavailable") --
#      the stock cu132 image does NOT: use the -io-uring derived image;
#   2. the container seccomp allows io_uring_setup/enter/register -- Docker's
#      default profile does not; seccomp-io-uring.json (byte-identical to
#      vllm scripts/seccomp/spark-io-uring.json) does;
#   3. the HOST allows io_uring: sysctl kernel.io_uring_disabled = 0.
#
# EVERY setting is explicit. Empty values are deliberate: "empty = the
# launcher omits the flag and the engine uses its own default" (or, for
# engine-read vars, the launcher's -e / the image's baked value applies).
#
# FORMAT RULES (the file is sourced by the launcher AND passed to --env-file):
#   - plain KEY=VALUE, no quotes; lists comma-separated, never spaces
#   - no JSON -- sourcing strips its quotes; the launcher builds JSON instead
#   - NEVER put a comment after a value: --env-file passes it into the container
#   - <placeholder> in a non-comment line is refused at --check
#
# Copy once per node; only section 1 differs between the two files:
#     cp mimo-v2.6-flash-rl_rank.env.example rank-0.env   # API node
#     cp mimo-v2.6-flash-rl_rank.env.example rank-1.env   # headless worker
# Validate: ./mimo-v2.6-flash-rl_pair-serve.sh --check rank-0.env
# Start rank 1 first (it blocks on rank 0's rendezvous), then rank 0.
# Quick restart with a clean page cache (previous model loads leave page
# cache that counts against CUDA free memory on GB10):
#     ./mimo-v2.6-flash-rl_pair-serve.sh --fresh rank-0.env
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
# 1. REQUIRED -- resolve every <placeholder>. Read from THIS host; never copy
#    fabric identity from another machine.
# =============================================================================

# 0 = API node (serves HTTP, coordinates); 1 = headless worker.
NODE_RANK=<0_or_1>

# Rank 0's IPv4 on the ConnectX-7 link. IDENTICAL in both files. The launcher
# dies if it routes through a gateway (a one-digit typo otherwise hangs both
# ranks forever with no error).
MASTER_ADDR=<rank0_fabric_ipv4>

# THIS node's IPv4 on the link. Rank 0: equal to MASTER_ADDR. Must be a local
# address -- this is what catches running the wrong rank's file.
VLLM_HOST_IP=<this_node_fabric_ipv4>

# Snapshot dir of XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.6-Flash-RL @ 3b38d063 holding config.json
# + model.safetensors.index.json + weights. Byte-identical on both nodes
# (rsync -c, or hash the files). Keep it on local NVMe; the load is NVMe-bound.
MODEL_HOST_PATH=<abs_path_to_model_snapshot>

# Writable JIT/compile cache, at least four directory levels deep (--clear
# wipes it and refuses shallow paths). Holds torch.compile, Triton,
# FlashInfer, B12X artifacts and the RoCEnante proxy. Use a directory distinct
# from the other models' caches.
CACHE_HOST_PATH=<abs_path_to_writable_cache>

# The kk-beta-cu132 image PLUS liburing-dev (see header). Build once:
#     docker build -f Dockerfile.io-uring -t local/vllm:karmic-kraken-beta-cu132-io-uring .
# then docker save | ssh <node2> docker load (identical image IDs).
SERVING_IMAGE=local/vllm:karmic-kraken-beta-cu132-io-uring

#   ip -br link  -> the interface on the CX7 link (NCCL and Gloo must match)
NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME=<fabric_ifname>
GLOO_SOCKET_IFNAME=<fabric_ifname>
#   ibv_devices  -> the RDMA device; exactly one under the single-rail profile
NCCL_IB_HCA=<rdma_device>
#   show_gids    -> the RoCEv2 IPv4 row's index. The #1 cause of silent NCCL
#   hangs when copied from another machine.
NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX=<rocev2_ipv4_gid_index>


# =============================================================================
# 2. SERVING SHAPE
# =============================================================================

# HTTP port on rank 0 / torch.distributed rendezvous port. Must differ.
API_PORT=8000
MASTER_PORT=29500

# Names clients may send, comma-separated, no spaces. The first is what
# /v1/models reports. (The catalog's name; the launcher's default matches.)
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=MiMo-V2.6-Flash-RL

# Empty = open port. Set to require Authorization: Bearer <key> on rank 0.
API_KEY=

# Speculator: none = the catalog-qualified default; mtp = the in-checkpoint
# MTP head (num_nextn_predict_layers; no extra weights -- the first A/B, add
# depth 3 and tune from there). dflash = DEFERRED (the pro-lineage path:
# separate draft snapshot + draft_tensor_parallel_size + the pooled-DFlash
# loading contract).
SPECULATOR=none

# MTP draft depth (only when SPECULATOR=mtp). Catalog default none; Luke's
# launcher starts 0. Start 3 (the GLM/Qwen qualified depth) and tune.
NUM_SPECULATIVE_TOKENS=

# Context ceiling. Groundwork value: 262144 (safe first boot). The
# checkpoint's ceiling is 1,048,576 and, by the header's KV math, one 1M
# request costs only ~11 GiB/rank of BF16 KV -- raise after the profiled
# boot confirms "GPU KV cache size" (bring-up order step 3). KK's own
# launcher runs auto (= 1,048,576) on TP4.
# MAX_MODEL_LEN=-1 = auto-fit to the KV pin (the launcher requires the pin
# for it and warns to pin the fitted value afterwards).
MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144

# Concurrent sequences. Catalog capacity: 4. A decode step under mtp is
# MAX_NUM_SEQS x (depth+1) tokens and must fit MAX_CUDAGRAPH_CAPTURE_SIZE.
MAX_NUM_SEQS=8

# Tokens per engine step = prefill chunk. Catalog 4096.
MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=8192

# Largest captured decode batch. Catalog TP1 runs 64 at 16 seqs; groundwork
# 16 covers 4 seqs x (3+1) with headroom.
MAX_CUDAGRAPH_CAPTURE_SIZE=32

# FULL_AND_PIECEWISE = the catalog compilation value.
CUDAGRAPH_MODE=FULL_AND_PIECEWISE

# custom_ops for the compilation config. Empty = the launcher omits the key
# and the engine default applies -- what KK's serve-mimo26-flash.sh does (it
# passes no compilation config at all). "none" would disable vLLM's custom
# CUDA ops on a graph-only run; set only for an A/B.
CUSTOM_OPS=

# Prefix cache reuse / chunked long prefills.
ENABLE_PREFIX_CACHING=1
ENABLE_CHUNKED_PREFILL=1

# Periodic SWA prefix-cache checkpoints -- POSSIBLE here (MiMo has SWA
# groups) but NOT in the catalog contract: leave empty (engine default 0 =
# semantic checkpoints only) for the groundwork; A/B 4096 later if prefix
# restoration granularity matters. Must be a BLOCK_SIZE multiple when set.
PREFIX_RETENTION_INTERVAL=

# 0: the checkpoint ships its tokenizer/config classes; the catalog sets it.
TRUST_REMOTE_CODE=1

# Public block-table unit. 128 = the catalog-qualified geometry for MiMo's
# 192-dim attention. GLM's 256 and Qwen's 64 are the wrong values here.
BLOCK_SIZE=128

# --- prefill/decode contention --------------------------------------------
# Empty = engine defaults on every qualified MiMo boot. The third-party
# attachment runs prefill-compute-share 0.8 (TP4) -- unmeasured here; the
# GLM pair's interval-8 is likewise an unmeasured import. A/B later.
PREFILL_SCHEDULE_INTERVAL=
FAIRNESS_ENGINE=
PREFILL_COMPUTE_SHARE=
PREFILL_COMPUTE_HALF_LIFE=
MAX_PARALLEL_PREFILLS=

# Async scheduling: NOT in the MiMo catalog contract (the Qwen/vision
# profiles set it; MiMo's does not). Leave empty for the groundwork.
ASYNC_SCHEDULING=


# =============================================================================
# 3. MEMORY
#
# Budget per rank: ~121.7 GiB unified, ~10.5 GiB held by the OS, plus the
# MXFP4-expert weights (TP=2 split), the image/video encoders, activations
# and graphs. The checkpoint's total byte size is TBD -- read it from the
# snapshot (du -sh) before the first boot. The KV pool is what remains.
# =============================================================================

# Pinned KV pool in bytes. EMPTY for the first boot: vLLM profiles at
# GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION and logs "Available KV cache memory" -- pin THAT
# number. MiMo's pool math has never been measured anywhere; the catalog
# runs unpinned at util 0.98 (an RTX value -- NOT valid here; GB10 refuses
# above ~0.913).
KV_CACHE_MEMORY_BYTES=

# Profiling fraction (the pool-sizing source while the pin is empty; the
# worker's request_memory() gate runs against it even after the pin is set).
GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.85

# bfloat16 = the catalog-qualified KV layout for MiMo's 192-dim attention.
# fp8 is UNVERIFIED on this model (A/B later with output checks).
KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8

# Host free-memory gate at --check (profiling mode only): die | warn | off.
MEM_PREFLIGHT=die

# cgroup cap so a runaway load kills the container, not the host.
CONTAINER_MEMORY_GB=


# =============================================================================
# 4. MULTIMODAL -- the checkpoint carries image + video encoders (audio via
#    the Omni override, not part of the groundwork)
# =============================================================================

# 0 = serve image/video (the catalog serves the full multimodal checkpoint).
LANGUAGE_MODEL_ONLY=0

# 1 = cap items per PROMPT (the whole chat history counts); 0 = engine
# default 999 per modality. Groundwork: 1 with the caps below (a TP2 pair
# has less headroom than the catalog's TP4 RTX box for uncapped histories).
LIMIT_MM=0

# Per-prompt caps when LIMIT_MM=1 (integers on purpose). Groundwork values;
# 0 disables a modality.
#MM_IMAGES=8
#MM_VIDEOS=0

# Host-RAM cache of preprocessed media: catalog multimodal value 0 (on
# unified memory the engine default 4 GiB/process is the same pool as KV).
MM_PROCESSOR_CACHE_GB=1

# weights = the catalog-qualified encoder TP mode (the ViT is TP-sharded;
# encoder collectives per image batch). data (each rank encodes its own
# items) duplicates ALL towers per rank -- on a TP2 pair that is ~2x the
# encoder memory; A/B only.
MM_ENCODER_TP_MODE=weights


# =============================================================================
# 5. KERNELS AND BACKENDS
# =============================================================================

# GB10 is sm_121. The launcher refuses anything else: sm_120a silently
# builds RTX Pro 6000 CuTeDSL kernels that compile and then fail at load.
# NOTE: the catalog REQUIRES arch sm_120a -- GB10/sm_121a is unqualified
# territory; expect kernel surprises at first boot.
CUTE_DSL_ARCH=sm_121a
FLASHINFER_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=12.1f

# Kernel backends: the catalog contract is b12x for attention, linear AND MoE.
MOE_BACKEND=b12x
ATTENTION_BACKEND=B12X
LINEAR_BACKEND=b12x

# FlashInfer startup autotune: catalog kernels.flashinfer_autotune false.
ENABLE_FLASHINFER_AUTOTUNE=0

# torch.compile level: empty = none (CUDA graphs only). A/B only.
COMPILATION_LEVEL=

# AOT compile artifacts: NOT in the MiMo catalog contract (Luke's launcher
# does not set them). Leave commented; A/B if boot time matters.
#VLLM_USE_AOT_COMPILE=1
#VLLM_USE_MEGA_AOT_ARTIFACT=1

# Quantization: auto = omit --quantization and let the checkpoint describe
# itself. CORRECTED 2026-09-23: the checkpoint is quant_method "fp8" with
# store_dtype "mxfp4" (block-FP8 projections, MXFP4 experts) -- NOT ModelOpt.
# modelopt_mixed fails vLLM's check ("Quantization method specified in the
# model config (fp8) does not match ... (modelopt_mixed)"). KK's launcher
# passes no --quantization.
QUANTIZATION=auto

# b12x preparation tuning search (b12x/preparation/session.py reads it;
# 0 skips tuning and uses cached/default selections).
B12X_AUTOTUNE=1

# Split-K with atomic BF16 accumulation for dense GEMMs (b12x default 1;
# now load-bearing at KK -- '0' or empty clamps split-k to 2 partials).
B12X_DENSE_SPLITK_TURBO=1

# b12x compile concurrency (default 8). 16 on the 20-core Grace, as on the
# other pair models. Identical on both ranks (part of the compile-cache key).
B12X_COMPILE_WORKERS=16

# 0 = FP4-activation MoE (catalog: the MXFP4 experts run the FP4 path);
# 1 = the older W4A16 path for an output-quality A/B.
VLLM_B12X_MOE_FP4_FORCE_A16=0

# Per-projection layer-max activation scales for NVFP4 MoE. CAUTION: never
# leave this line EMPTY-valued -- the engine's env_with_choices validates
# the empty string and crashes boot. Unmeasured on MiMo; A/B before trusting.
VLLM_B12X_MOE_FP4_LAYER_MAX_INPUT_SCALE=0

# NOT carried (zero read sites at these pins, verified 2026-09-23):
# VLLM_USE_B12X_MOE / _FP8_GEMM / _SPARSE_INDEXER / _MHC / _WO_PROJECTION /
# _DCP_A2A, B12X_MOE_FORCE_A8, B12X_W4A16_TC_DECODE, B12X_MLA_SM120_UNIFIED
# (the third-party attachment's B12X_W4A16_FP32_TOPK_WEIGHTS is likewise not
# registered on this line). B12X_POLICY_MODE: retired at b12x 77351c13.
# VLLM_B12X_MOE_FP4_LAYER_MAX_INPUT_SCALE targets NVFP4 MoE; MiMo's experts
# are MXFP4, so it is expected to be inert here (kept at the safe 0).
#
# NOT applicable to this model (do not port from the GLM/Qwen files):
# REPLAYSSM (recovery eligibility is Glm5Next/Kimi only -- Qwen/MiMo auto-
# resolve OFF), VLLM_SSM_CONV_STATE_LAYOUT (no mamba/GDN state), KDA_*/GDN_*
# backends (no KDA layers), RECURRENT_CHECKPOINT_POLICY (no recurrent state),
# VLLM_GLM53_* (GLM-only levers), VLLM_QWEN3_8_* (Qwen-only levers).

# KV cache layout: engine auto -- so the key is ABSENT. An empty
# VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT= reaches the container as '' and the engine's
# env_with_choices raises "Invalid value ''" at startup. BLHNC (block-
# outermost) is needed ONLY when mixing draft+target page sizes (the DFlash
# A/B; fc27214ba9). To set it, uncomment:
#VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT=BLHNC

# Fully offline: the model resolves from the mount only.
HF_HOME=/root/.cache/huggingface
HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1
TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1
VLLM_NO_USAGE_STATS=1

# The b12x loader REQUIRES the plugin; the launcher dies without it.
VLLM_PLUGINS=b12x_loader
# fork + CUDA is unsafe; spawn is required.
VLLM_WORKER_MULTIPROC_METHOD=spawn

# Compat shim FIRST (image kernels are CUDA 13.2; the host driver exports
# older -- without it every process dies at import with "undefined symbol:
# cuTensorMapEncodeTiled"), then the patched NCCL for the switchless pair.
# The launcher verifies both paths exist inside the image.
LD_PRELOAD=/usr/local/cuda/compat/libcuda.so.1:/opt/libnccl-local-inference.so.2.30.4
VLLM_NCCL_SO_PATH=/opt/libnccl-local-inference.so.2.30.4
NCCL_LOCAL_INFERENCE_PATH=/opt/libnccl-local-inference.so.2.30.4
NCCL_PR2127_PATH=/opt/libnccl-local-inference.so.2.30.4
TORCH_USE_RTLD_GLOBAL=1

# JIT toolchain: Triton uses the image's CUDA 13.2 ptxas, not its bundled one.
CUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda
TRITON_PTXAS_PATH=/usr/local/cuda/bin/ptxas

# Allocator: expandable segments, required alongside NCCL_CUMEM_ENABLE=0.
PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True
CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID
CUDA_DEVICE_MAX_CONNECTIONS=32

# Grace CPU threads for torch (the pair convention; Luke's TP4 launcher
# runs 16 -- unmeasured here).
OMP_NUM_THREADS=2

# docker or podman.
CONTAINER_RUNTIME=docker
# Optional suffix so two env files can run side by side on one host (A/B).
CONTAINER_NAME_SUFFIX=

# Container seccomp: REQUIRED for the b12x loader's io_uring ring. The
# shipped profile = Moby default + io_uring_setup/enter/register (identical
# to vllm scripts/seccomp/spark-io-uring.json). A relative name resolves next
# to the launcher, so keep the .json in this model directory. unconfined =
# last resort (drops every syscall filter). Empty = runtime default, which
# blocks io_uring on Docker >= 25 (the launcher's probe dies with the fix).
SECCOMP_PROFILE=seccomp-io-uring.json


# =============================================================================
# 6. COLLECTIVES -- RoCEnante (b12x one-shot RoCE collectives)
# =============================================================================

# 1 routes TP all-reduces <= ALLREDUCE_MAX_SIZE and all-gather shards <=
# ALLGATHER_MAX_SIZE through b12x.comm.roce; NCCL keeps the rest. 16 MiB is
# the pair-qualified value on GLM/Qwen (Luke's launcher and the eugr recipes
# run 2 MB); unmeasured on MiMo -- carried as the pair convention. The proxy
# compiles at first boot into B12X_ROCE_CACHE_DIR (keep under /cache).
VLLM_ENABLE_ROCE_ALLREDUCE=1
VLLM_ROCE_ALLREDUCE_MAX_SIZE=16777216
VLLM_ROCE_ALLGATHER_MAX_SIZE=16777216
B12X_ROCE_CACHE_DIR=/cache/jit/b12x-roce

# The B12X PCIe allreduce is a single-node PCIe P2P path; the image bakes 1,
# this overrides to 0 and the launcher refuses 1.
VLLM_ENABLE_PCIE_ALLREDUCE=0


# =============================================================================
# 7. FABRIC -- RoCEv2 over the direct link; launcher-enforced
# =============================================================================

# RoCE presents IB semantics over Ethernet: IB is correct. The image bakes
# NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1 for single-node boxes; this overrides it.
NCCL_NET=IB
NCCL_NET_PLUGIN=none
NCCL_TUNER_PLUGIN=none
NCCL_IB_DISABLE=0

# Single-path: 0/0 (validated on the GLM pair).
# Fabric profiles (measured 2026-09-21, Luke's launchers):
#   single-path (validated on this pair): MERGE_NICS=0, one HCA in
#     NCCL_IB_HCA, one cable.
#   dual-path (Luke's Spark launchers): MERGE_NICS=1 with BOTH Linux
#     interfaces of the cabled port in NCCL_IB_HCA (rocep1s0f0,roceP2p1s0f0)
#     -- the two PCIe Gen5 x4 paths into the SAME CX-7, not a second cable:
#     one 200G link striped over both PCIe paths (196 Gb/s combined vs the
#     single-path cap). The second interface needs its own IPv4 (own /24) so
#     the GID index is populated on both; RoCEnante picks up to two HCAs.
#     SUBNET_AWARE_ROUTING is no longer part of that profile (dropped
#     upstream at 9e5d179); it only matters behind a switch.
NCCL_IB_SUBNET_AWARE_ROUTING=0
NCCL_IB_MERGE_NICS=0

# Qualified protocol/topology set for the direct-cable pair.
NCCL_PROTO=LL,LL128,Simple
NCCL_P2P_LEVEL=SYS
NCCL_CROSS_NIC=1

# NCCL's CUDA VMM allocator conflicts with expandable_segments: keep 0.
NCCL_CUMEM_ENABLE=0

# Grace's unified layout defeats NCCL's NUMA guesses.
NCCL_IGNORE_CPU_AFFINITY=1

# WARN for serving. INFO names the transport per channel (NET/IB vs
# NET/Socket) when debugging a hang or confirming RoCE is in use.
NCCL_DEBUG=WARN


# =============================================================================
# BRING-UP ORDER (record every number in the header when done)
#
# 1. du -sh the snapshot; confirm the TP2 weight split fits the pair budget
#    (121.7 GiB/rank minus OS minus encoders/activations).
# 2. --check both ranks: confirm the b12x loader plugin line, the io_uring
#    probe passing, BF16 KV, block 128, and no speculation in the command.
# 3. Profile boot: KV_CACHE_MEMORY_BYTES empty, util 0.90, vision ON. Take
#    from the rank-0 log: "Available KV cache memory" -> the byte pin;
#    "GPU KV cache size: N tokens"; "Maximum concurrency for L tokens".
# 4. Pin the bytes. THEN raise MAX_MODEL_LEN 262144 -> 1048576 while the
#    token count covers it (the checkpoint ceiling).
# 5. --verify on BOTH ranks: MiMo model class, b12x attention/linear/MoE
#    lines, "Graph capturing finished". A server that answers /health can
#    still be on a fallback path.
# 6. ONE knob per boot, in this order of expected payoff: SPECULATOR=mtp
#    depth 3 (the in-checkpoint head); MM_ENCODER_TP_MODE=data (memory
#    win if the encoders fit); fp8 KV (quality-check outputs!);
#    prefill-compute-share A/B; ASYNC_SCHEDULING=1.
# 7. Any change of speculator, vision mode, loader, or pin invalidates 3-4:
#    re-measure. A benchmark JSON and an env file describing different
#    boots are never published together.
# =============================================================================
